          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Could this occur when using the formula ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\frac12 ab\\sin C",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. For a triangle, $0^\\circ<C<180^\\circ$, so $\\sin C>0$. The side lengths $a$ and $b$ are also positive.",
      "worked": "No. An obtuse angle has negative cosine, but every interior triangle angle satisfies $0^\\circ<C<180^\\circ$, so $\\sin C>0$. Since $a>0$ and $b>0$, the product $\\tfrac12 ab\\sin C$ is positive.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
